1
00:00:03,770 --> 00:00:05,830
Oh, my God. I love this chicken.

2
00:00:05,830 --> 00:00:07,610
Oh, you know what they say,

3
00:00:07,610 --> 00:00:09,850
best things in life are free.

4
00:00:10,990 --> 00:00:12,700
Okay, you're right. I eat your food a lot.

5
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,240
Now, how about this?

6
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:15,360
You can raid my fridge anytime you want.

7
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:17,200
Oh, that's very kind of you.

8
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,410
Next time I have a hankering to wash down a D-cell battery

9
00:00:20,410 --> 00:00:22,310
with a jar of old pickle juice,

10
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:23,760
I'll come a-knockin'.

11
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:27,220
Hey, Raj, you didn't send your RSVP in.

12
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:30,100
I'm suppose to ask you if you're bringing someone to the wedding.

13
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:31,130
I'll let you know.

14
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:32,010
Well, can you make it soon?

15
00:00:32,010 --> 00:00:34,500
There's a battle royale going on over the seating charts.

16
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,150
In one corner, Bernadette's mom,

17
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:38,190
in the other three, mine.

18
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:41,120
Yeah, I hate wedding receptions.

19
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:44,050
Yeah, I wish the bride and groom would take a cue from Bilbo Baggins.

20
00:00:44,060 --> 00:00:47,110
Slip on the ring, disappear, and everyone goes home.

21
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:50,610
Mm, you liked Professor Geyser's wedding.

22
00:00:50,610 --> 00:00:53,140
They had a make-your-own-sundae bar.

23
00:00:53,140 --> 00:00:55,160
Oh, that was a night to remember.

24
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:58,480
Do you know, on one trip, I just had a bowl of nuts.

25
00:00:59,790 --> 00:01:02,420
Anyway, you got to let me know if you have a plus one.

26
00:01:02,430 --> 00:01:04,710
Because if not, my mom's trying to sneak in the doctor

27
00:01:04,710 --> 00:01:06,830
who sucked the fat out of her neck.

28
00:01:11,030 --> 00:01:12,100
All right, uh, fine.

29
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:14,100
I'm coming and I'm bringing somebody.

30
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:15,780
Uh, Koothrappali plus one.

31
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:16,470
Who you bringing?

32
00:01:16,470 --> 00:01:17,830
Who are you bringing?!

33
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:20,870
He's bringing me; who are you bringing?

34
00:01:21,090 --> 00:01:24,190
Wow, what a bunch of Nosey O'Donnells.

35
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:26,690
Come on, who is it?

36
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:27,910
I'm not telling.

37
00:01:27,910 --> 00:01:30,980
I'm from Asia, I'm mysterious, deal with it.

38
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:35,220
Howard aren't having a make-your-own-sundae bar?

39
00:01:35,390 --> 00:01:36,780
I don't think so.

40
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:37,740
Well, you should.

41
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:39,980
50% of marriages end in divorce,

42
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:43,430
but 100% of make-your-own-sundae bars end in happiness.

43
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:13,680
Hello, Mummy, Daddy. How are you?

44
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:15,980
Pretty good. Can't complain.

45
00:02:16,150 --> 00:02:17,120
Oh, I'm sure you can.

46
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,640
Just give it a minute.

47
00:02:20,230 --> 00:02:21,540
Listen, uh,

48
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:23,490
there's something I want to talk to you about.

49
00:02:23,490 --> 00:02:26,390
I wasn't ready until now, but...

50
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:27,990
I think it's time.

51
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:29,290
It's finally happening.

52
00:02:29,290 --> 00:02:31,590
You're coming out of the closet, aren't you?

53
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:35,780
We love you, and we accept your alternate lifestyle.

54
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:38,430
Just... keep it to yourself.

55
00:02:39,650 --> 00:02:41,980
No, I'm not gay.

56
00:02:42,270 --> 00:02:44,750
If anything, I'm metrosexual.

57
00:02:45,310 --> 00:02:46,450
What's that?

58
00:02:46,590 --> 00:02:49,940
It means I like women as well as their skin-care products.

59
00:02:50,630 --> 00:02:51,700
Well, if you're not coming out,

60
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:54,680
why did you call us during the cricket semifinals?

61
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:58,030
I'm tired of trying to meet someone,

62
00:02:58,030 --> 00:03:01,380
and I think I'd like you to help me find a...

63
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:03,160
a wife.

64
00:03:03,810 --> 00:03:05,350
And just to clarify...

65
00:03:05,350 --> 00:03:07,310
a female wife?

66
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:09,010
Yes!

67
00:03:09,650 --> 00:03:12,380
Matchmaking-- very smart move, son.

68
00:03:12,390 --> 00:03:14,910
Much better than marrying for love.

69
00:03:20,030 --> 00:03:22,240
We married for love.

70
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:25,330
And it's been wonderful!

71
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:31,120
Quantum physics makes me so happy.

72
00:03:32,390 --> 00:03:33,730
Yeah, I'm glad.

73
00:03:33,730 --> 00:03:35,910
It's like looking at the universe naked.

74
00:03:45,170 --> 00:03:46,270
Hi. Guys got a minute?

75
00:03:46,270 --> 00:03:47,600
Sure. What's up?

76
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:50,050
Well, I was thinking about Sheldon's little joke

77
00:03:50,050 --> 00:03:51,800
the other night about me eating all your food.

78
00:03:51,810 --> 00:03:54,140
Oh! That was no joke. But...

79
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,030
I understand your confusion,

80
00:03:56,030 --> 00:03:58,580
as I am our group's resident cutup.

81
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:03,180
I'm sorry, you are our resident cutup?

82
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:04,880
Yes.

83
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,540
Oh, prove it.

84
00:04:07,650 --> 00:04:08,260
Knock-knock.

85
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:09,770
- Who's there? - Interrupting physicist.

86
00:04:09,770 --> 00:04:13,030
- Interrupting phys... - Muon!

87
00:04:15,470 --> 00:04:18,520
Anyway, I got a little residual check from my commercial,

88
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:20,220
and I thought, hey, how about I get the guys

89
00:04:20,220 --> 00:04:22,510
a little thank you to pay them back?

90
00:04:22,510 --> 00:04:23,910
So, Sheldon...

91
00:04:24,270 --> 00:04:25,640
ta-da!

92
00:04:26,390 --> 00:04:27,990
A vintage mint-in-box

93
00:04:27,990 --> 00:04:30,930
1975 Mego Star Trek Transporter

94
00:04:30,930 --> 00:04:32,490
with real transporter action.

95
00:04:32,490 --> 00:04:33,660
Hot darn!

96
00:04:35,570 --> 00:04:36,770
Where did you get that?

97
00:04:36,770 --> 00:04:38,460
From Stuart, at the comic book store.

98
00:04:38,460 --> 00:04:40,930
You went to the comic book store by yourself?

99
00:04:40,930 --> 00:04:42,950
Yeah. It was fun.

100
00:04:42,950 --> 00:04:45,780
I walked in, and two different guys got asthma attacks.

101
00:04:47,950 --> 00:04:49,340
Felt pretty good.

102
00:04:49,950 --> 00:04:52,110
This calls for an expression of gratitude.

103
00:04:52,110 --> 00:04:54,670
Ooh, am I about to get a rare Sheldon Cooper hug?

104
00:04:54,670 --> 00:04:57,050
No, not this time. Then they wouldn't be special.

105
00:04:57,650 --> 00:04:58,830
Thanks, Penny.

106
00:05:00,510 --> 00:05:01,880
You're welcome.

107
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:04,990
Don't worry, I didn't forget about you.

108
00:05:05,190 --> 00:05:06,970
Leonard, I got you...

109
00:05:06,970 --> 00:05:09,700
a label-maker!

110
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:17,460
Wow...

111
00:05:18,410 --> 00:05:19,530
No, it's great.

112
00:05:19,530 --> 00:05:22,610
Also mint-in-box. Mm.

113
00:05:23,150 --> 00:05:25,090
And I got you a transporter, too!

114
00:05:25,090 --> 00:05:26,950
Awesome!

115
00:05:30,430 --> 00:05:34,060
Look, it was actually designed for my vintage Mr. Spock action figure.

116
00:05:34,060 --> 00:05:36,080
Oh, that's great! Let's open them up and put him in there.

117
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:37,870
- Open it?! - Oh, good Lord, no!

118
00:05:39,170 --> 00:05:40,380
Why? They're just toys.

119
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:42,300
- They're collectibles. - They're mint-in-box.

120
00:05:42,870 --> 00:05:44,190
Come on. Can't we open one up and take a look?

121
00:05:44,190 --> 00:05:45,670
No, don't!

122
00:05:46,570 --> 00:05:49,590
Once you open the box, it loses its value.

123
00:05:49,590 --> 00:05:53,070
Yeah, yeah. My mom gave me the same lecture about my virginity.

124
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:56,970
Gotta tell you, it was a lot more fun

125
00:05:56,970 --> 00:05:58,970
taking it out and playing with it.

126
00:06:02,350 --> 00:06:04,850
Are you sure you want us here when you meet this woman?

127
00:06:04,870 --> 00:06:05,600
Oh, yes.

128
00:06:05,610 --> 00:06:06,640
In my culture, it's expected

129
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:09,140
to have a chaperone to oversee a first date.

130
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:11,350
Plus, I want to make a good impression, and no offense,

131
00:06:11,350 --> 00:06:14,630
but with you guys here, I look like I'm six-two.

132
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:19,710
The nuns always chaperoned the dances at my high school.

133
00:06:19,710 --> 00:06:22,970
They used to make us leave room between us for the Holy Spirit.

134
00:06:23,870 --> 00:06:25,170
Uh, Hindus do the same thing.

135
00:06:25,170 --> 00:06:27,250
Except they leave room for a cow.

136
00:06:29,050 --> 00:06:31,320
Listen, I love your charming racist humor,

137
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:34,470
but any chance you could not mock my religion while she's here?

138
00:06:34,470 --> 00:06:36,300
Yesterday, you made fun of me for eating lox.

139
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:38,510
It's different, your people don't worship lox.

140
00:06:38,510 --> 00:06:40,640
Clearly, you've never been to brunch with my cousins.

141
00:06:42,220 --> 00:06:44,360
So, arranged marriages-- the parents just decide

142
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:46,200
and then you have to get married?

143
00:06:46,210 --> 00:06:47,990
No, no, I get a say in it.

144
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:49,950
But I'm sure whoever shows up will be better company

145
00:06:49,950 --> 00:06:51,060
than the threesome I've been having

146
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:53,610
with Aunt Jemima and Mrs. Butterworth.

147
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:57,560
Excuse me, are you Rajesh?

148
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:58,790
Ah, yes.

149
00:06:58,910 --> 00:07:00,050
You must be Lakshmi.

150
00:07:00,050 --> 00:07:01,040
Uh, nice to meet you.

151
00:07:01,050 --> 00:07:02,580
Nice to meet you, too.

152
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:04,940
Oh! These are my friends.

153
00:07:04,940 --> 00:07:06,450
- This is Bernadette. - Hello.

154
00:07:06,450 --> 00:07:08,180
- And this is Howard. - Nice to meet you.

155
00:07:08,190 --> 00:07:10,280
- You, too. - Please, have a seat.

156
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:13,700
I'm thinking double wedding.

157
00:07:18,270 --> 00:07:19,780
Dr. Cooper.

158
00:07:22,910 --> 00:07:24,160
Dr. Cooper?

159
00:07:26,210 --> 00:07:27,550
Is someone there?

160
00:07:27,650 --> 00:07:30,240
Down here. On your desk.

161
00:07:34,510 --> 00:07:35,410
Spock?

162
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:37,520
I need to speak with you.

163
00:07:39,110 --> 00:07:41,570
Fascinating.

164
00:07:41,570 --> 00:07:44,740
The only logical explanation is that this is a dream.

165
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:47,950
It is not the only logical explanation.

166
00:07:47,950 --> 00:07:50,340
For example, you could be hallucinating

167
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:52,430
after being hit on the head by,say,

168
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:54,150
a coconut.

169
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:58,880
Was I hit on the head by a coconut?

170
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:01,770
I am not going to dignify that with a response.

171
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:04,870
Now to the matter at hand.

172
00:08:04,870 --> 00:08:07,810
You need to play with the transporter toy.

173
00:08:07,810 --> 00:08:09,470
But it's mint-in-box.

174
00:08:09,470 --> 00:08:10,210
Yes.

175
00:08:10,210 --> 00:08:12,660
And to open it would destroy its value.

176
00:08:12,770 --> 00:08:14,310
But remember, like me,

177
00:08:15,690 --> 00:08:17,910
you also have a human half.

178
00:08:18,090 --> 00:08:20,910
Well, I'm not going to dignify that with a response.

179
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:23,060
Consider this.

180
00:08:24,050 --> 00:08:25,590
What is the purpose of a toy?

181
00:08:25,590 --> 00:08:27,070
To be played with.

182
00:08:27,070 --> 00:08:30,270
Therefore, to not play with it would be...?

183
00:08:30,270 --> 00:08:31,280
Illogical.

184
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:33,170
Damn it, Spock, you're right.

185
00:08:35,170 --> 00:08:36,490
I'll do it.

186
00:08:36,570 --> 00:08:39,030
Sheldon, wait.

187
00:08:39,850 --> 00:08:41,790
You have to wake up first.

188
00:08:41,790 --> 00:08:43,310
Oh, of course.

189
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:46,020
Set phasers to dumb, right?

190
00:08:47,910 --> 00:08:49,420
Goodie, goodie, goodie!

191
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:53,420
This is wrong, this is wrong.

192
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:55,460
I'm so excited, but this is wrong.

193
00:08:58,890 --> 00:09:00,350
I'm going to do it.

194
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:02,270
I'm doing it.

195
00:09:02,850 --> 00:09:04,020
I did it.

196
00:09:09,210 --> 00:09:12,110
That's what I always thought 1975 smelled like.

197
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:18,550
One to beam down, Mr. Scott.

198
00:09:18,550 --> 00:09:20,490
Aye, aye, Mr. Spock.

199
00:09:20,590 --> 00:09:22,070
Energize.

200
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,530
Energize.

201
00:09:39,570 --> 00:09:40,870
Don't be broken.

202
00:09:41,470 --> 00:09:43,550
Oh, please, don't be broken.

203
00:09:45,310 --> 00:09:46,790
What did you make me do?!

204
00:09:48,890 --> 00:09:51,770
Okay, okay, think.

205
00:09:58,430 --> 00:10:00,110
It's only logical.

206
00:10:04,790 --> 00:10:07,150
My goodness, that was delicious.

207
00:10:07,150 --> 00:10:11,400
Well, I hope you saved room for chocolate lava cake.

208
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:13,020
Impressive.

209
00:10:13,020 --> 00:10:15,240
What goes into making something like that?

210
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:16,860
Well, you start out by trying to

211
00:10:16,860 --> 00:10:19,780
make chocolate souffl? And when it falls, you panic,

212
00:10:19,780 --> 00:10:22,870
quickly change the name, and voila, lava cake.

213
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:26,860
I bet our parents are dying to know how things are going here.

214
00:10:26,870 --> 00:10:28,930
Well, let's see.

215
00:10:30,670 --> 00:10:32,280
Yep, three missed calls.

216
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:34,040
Four missed calls, two text messages

217
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:36,420
and a failed video chat. I win!

218
00:10:37,690 --> 00:10:40,490
So, what are we going to tell them?

219
00:10:41,130 --> 00:10:43,110
I'd like to tell them things are going well.

220
00:10:43,110 --> 00:10:44,220
Me, too.

221
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:45,780
But before we get their hopes up,

222
00:10:45,790 --> 00:10:48,840
we should probably make sure we're on the same page.

223
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:50,420
Okay.

224
00:10:50,580 --> 00:10:52,430
What page are you on?

225
00:10:53,130 --> 00:10:56,010
I'm on the one where I'm under a lot of pressure

226
00:10:56,010 --> 00:10:58,650
from my parents to get married and settle down

227
00:10:58,650 --> 00:10:59,920
and have a family,

228
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:02,690
and I'm going to do it so they don't find out I'm gay.

229
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:07,040
Say again?

230
00:11:07,830 --> 00:11:08,990
I'm gay.

231
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:11,800
Like... dude-on-dude,

232
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:13,380
but with women?

233
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:16,990
I know a fake marriage isn't an honest way to live,

234
00:11:16,990 --> 00:11:18,930
but you of all people should know how difficult it is

235
00:11:18,930 --> 00:11:20,760
to come out in our culture.

236
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:23,230
Why me of all people?!

237
00:11:23,630 --> 00:11:26,440
Well, there's a rumor back in New Delhi that you're--

238
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:27,840
how shall we say--

239
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:29,860
comfortable in a sari.

240
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:32,300
I'm not gay!

241
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:34,690
Really? The chocolate lava cake,

242
00:11:34,690 --> 00:11:36,120
the little soaps in the bathroom,

243
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:39,060
and I'm sorry, but you're wearing more perfume than I am.

244
00:11:40,010 --> 00:11:43,060
That's Unbreakable by Khloe and Lamar.

245
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:46,430
And for your information, it's unisex.

246
00:11:47,610 --> 00:11:48,760
Fill in the blank.

247
00:11:48,770 --> 00:11:50,150
I love the nightlife...

248
00:11:50,150 --> 00:11:51,460
I like to boogie.

249
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:52,490
Got you.

250
00:11:52,490 --> 00:11:55,230
With women! I like to boogie with women!

251
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:58,000
That's disappointing.

252
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,380
You were exactly the kind of phony-baloney husband

253
00:12:00,380 --> 00:12:02,010
I was looking for.

254
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:03,980
Thank you.

255
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:06,710
And once again, my baloney likes girls.

256
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:10,350
W-W-Wait!

257
00:12:10,350 --> 00:12:12,150
You don't want to put a bite of that in your mouth

258
00:12:12,150 --> 00:12:15,160
without trying my homemade Chantilly cream.

259
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,220
Yeah, okay, that time I heard it.

260
00:12:31,490 --> 00:12:33,200
Oh, dear.

261
00:12:34,510 --> 00:12:37,780
Two suns and no sunscreen.

262
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:44,240
Hello again, Sheldon.

263
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:48,110
What is it now, Tiny Spock?

264
00:12:48,370 --> 00:12:50,640
I am very disappointed in you.

265
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:53,300
You broke your toy and switched it with Leonard's.

266
00:12:53,300 --> 00:12:55,620
You should be ashamed of yourself.

267
00:12:55,620 --> 00:12:57,940
You're the one who told me to play with it.

268
00:12:57,940 --> 00:13:00,540
If I told you to jump off the bridge of the Enterprise,

269
00:13:00,540 --> 00:13:01,800
would you do it?

270
00:13:02,370 --> 00:13:04,990
Oh, if I got on the bridge of the Enterprise,

271
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,270
I would never, ever leave.

272
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:11,440
Trust me, it gets old after a while.

273
00:13:13,300 --> 00:13:15,400
You must right your wrongs, Sheldon.

274
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:17,910
Why? I got away with it.

275
00:13:17,910 --> 00:13:21,150
Leonard has his toy, and he's never going to open it,

276
00:13:21,150 --> 00:13:22,540
so he won't know it's broken.

277
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:24,870
And I have a toy that isn't broken.

278
00:13:24,870 --> 00:13:26,110
Everybody's happy.

279
00:13:26,110 --> 00:13:28,020
Well, I am unhappy.

280
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:30,910
I thought where you come from they don't have emotions.

281
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:34,950
I come from a factory in Taiwan.

282
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:38,000
Now, do the right thing.

283
00:13:38,370 --> 00:13:39,910
You know what you are?

284
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:42,530
Well, you're a green-blooded buzz kill.

285
00:13:43,170 --> 00:13:45,230
Perhaps it's time you beam on out of here.

286
00:13:45,230 --> 00:13:46,140
Fine.

287
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:48,300
I will just use the transporter.

288
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:49,950
Oh, right.

289
00:13:49,950 --> 00:13:51,750
You broke it.

290
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:54,680
Very well.

291
00:13:54,750 --> 00:13:57,980
Cooper to Enterprise, one to beam up.

292
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:59,850
Energize.

293
00:14:10,950 --> 00:14:13,060
Tiny Spock, help.

294
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:19,860
Ready for lunch?

295
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:21,180
Yeah, one sec.

296
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:24,010
Oh, good. Ma would've killed me

297
00:14:24,010 --> 00:14:26,250
if she found out I broke my retainer.

298
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:32,200
Can I run something by you? It's about Lakshmi.

299
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:34,300
Yeah, sure. How are things going?

300
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:35,830
We hit a couple of bumps.

301
00:14:35,830 --> 00:14:37,230
She lives over in Manhattan Beach,

302
00:14:37,230 --> 00:14:39,290
so it takes, like, an hour to get there.

303
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:41,120
And she's a lesbian.

304
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:44,880
What do you mean, "she's a lesbian"?

305
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:47,180
Well, you know how whenever you and I would try

306
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:49,150
to hit on women in bars and they'd blow us off

307
00:14:49,150 --> 00:14:51,770
and then we'd tell each other they were probably gay?

308
00:14:51,770 --> 00:14:52,950
It's like that.

309
00:14:53,130 --> 00:14:54,890
Except this time, it's true.

310
00:14:56,620 --> 00:14:58,780
Then why did she even go out with you?

311
00:14:58,780 --> 00:15:01,840
She was looking for a husband so she can appear to be straight.

312
00:15:01,950 --> 00:15:02,680
And, you know,

313
00:15:02,680 --> 00:15:04,740
it sounded crazy to me at first...

314
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:08,230
but I'm actually thinking about doing it.

315
00:15:09,020 --> 00:15:12,220
Okay, so the reason that might sound crazy...

316
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:13,710
is 'cause it's crazy!

317
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:17,030
Look, Howard, you're in a relationship.

318
00:15:17,030 --> 00:15:18,750
You know you have to make compromises.

319
00:15:18,750 --> 00:15:22,440
Yes, but my compromises are about which bedspread to buy

320
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:24,460
or whose turn it is to do the laundry,

321
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:26,360
Bernadette's or my mom's.

322
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:31,050
It's a great deal.

323
00:15:31,050 --> 00:15:33,140
We both get our parents off our backs,

324
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:35,670
I don't have to come home to an empty apartment every night.

325
00:15:35,670 --> 00:15:38,460
Plus, once I'm married, I can finally eat carbs again

326
00:15:38,460 --> 00:15:40,540
and let myself go.

327
00:15:41,540 --> 00:15:43,400
Why don't you tell your parents

328
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:45,770
you want to try to find someone else?

329
00:15:45,770 --> 00:15:49,120
Maybe one who hasn't slept with more woman than you.

330
00:15:49,870 --> 00:15:52,010
Because this one wants to marry me.

331
00:15:52,010 --> 00:15:54,210
I might never find another one who does.

332
00:15:54,210 --> 00:15:56,600
So you're seriously thinking about marrying someone

333
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:58,870
you're never gonna have sex with?

334
00:15:59,270 --> 00:16:00,550
I can't believe your attitude.

335
00:16:00,550 --> 00:16:03,530
I thought you were in favor of gay people getting married.

336
00:16:05,050 --> 00:16:07,260
Yes, to other gay people!

337
00:16:08,350 --> 00:16:10,760
Do you hear how homophobic you sound?

338
00:16:51,980 --> 00:16:54,260
Oh, I don't want a broken toy.

339
00:16:57,730 --> 00:16:58,880
Nothing!

340
00:17:01,390 --> 00:17:01,950
What?

341
00:17:01,950 --> 00:17:03,660
Nothing. I said nothing.

342
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:05,290
That was weird.

343
00:17:05,290 --> 00:17:07,390
Really? I don't even notice anymore.

344
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:11,600
I cannot believe you guys aren't gonna play with these.

345
00:17:11,600 --> 00:17:14,140
Well, I told you, you don't. It's mint-in-box.

346
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:16,860
I don't know. I just think it's a waste.

347
00:17:22,180 --> 00:17:24,320
Relax. I'm just looking at the box.

348
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:26,060
Perhaps you should look with your eyes

349
00:17:26,070 --> 00:17:29,060
and not your muscular Nebraska man hands.

350
00:17:30,770 --> 00:17:32,150
What is your problem?!

351
00:17:32,150 --> 00:17:35,680
My problem is that I don't want you to break Leonard's toy.

352
00:17:35,690 --> 00:17:37,410
Which you probably did by shaking it!

353
00:17:37,410 --> 00:17:39,230
She shook it, we all saw her.

354
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:41,880
Leonard, I bought you this

355
00:17:41,880 --> 00:17:43,890
'cause I wanted you to have fun with it.

356
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:46,040
I don't want it to sit in this box.

357
00:17:46,580 --> 00:17:48,710
You know, you're right.

358
00:17:48,870 --> 00:17:50,120
I mean, it's from you,

359
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:51,780
I'm never gonna sell it.

360
00:17:52,100 --> 00:17:53,800
- I'm opening it. - Yes!

361
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:07,070
- It's broken. - What?

362
00:18:07,070 --> 00:18:09,210
Oh, nice job, man hands!

363
00:18:11,290 --> 00:18:12,760
I didn't break it.

364
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:15,390
I guess Stuart sold it to me like this.

365
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:17,590
Yes. Yes, he did.

366
00:18:17,590 --> 00:18:21,020
That is a perfectly satisfying and plausible explana...

367
00:18:21,020 --> 00:18:23,060
Let's all be mad at Stuart!

368
00:18:24,170 --> 00:18:25,750
You know, I paid a lot for this.

369
00:18:25,750 --> 00:18:27,060
Let's take it over there and show him.

370
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:28,440
Absolutely.

371
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:32,460
Wait!

372
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:37,330
It was me.

373
00:18:38,120 --> 00:18:40,130
I opened your toy...

374
00:18:40,810 --> 00:18:43,410
discovered it was broken and didn't tell you.

375
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:47,120
Why would you open mine?

376
00:18:47,250 --> 00:18:48,800
I didn't. That was a lie.

377
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:52,030
I opened my own toy...

378
00:18:52,390 --> 00:18:55,230
and it was already broken, so I switched them.

379
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:57,820
You should talk to Stuart.

380
00:18:57,820 --> 00:18:59,590
I can't, because that was a lie.

381
00:19:01,190 --> 00:19:04,370
Yours was broken in an earthquake--

382
00:19:04,370 --> 00:19:05,610
and that's a lie.

383
00:19:08,290 --> 00:19:10,160
What is the truth?

384
00:19:11,230 --> 00:19:12,740
My Mr. Spock doll came to me in a dream

385
00:19:12,740 --> 00:19:14,220
and forced me to open it.

386
00:19:14,220 --> 00:19:18,140
And when the toy broke, I switched it for yours.

387
00:19:18,470 --> 00:19:20,150
Later, he encouraged me to do the right thing,

388
00:19:20,150 --> 00:19:21,690
and I defied him.

389
00:19:22,030 --> 00:19:23,980
And then I was attacked by a Gorn.

390
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:30,550
Okay, that I believe.

391
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:33,490
Leonard, Penny, I just, I want you both to know

392
00:19:33,490 --> 00:19:36,060
that I regret my actions towards the two of you.

393
00:19:36,060 --> 00:19:37,310
That's a lie.

394
00:19:39,140 --> 00:19:40,910
So, is that one mine?

395
00:19:41,410 --> 00:19:43,860
- Yes. - Well, hand it over so I can open it.

396
00:19:44,150 --> 00:19:45,220
Okay.

397
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:48,530
And, Leonard, even though I don't have one anymore,

398
00:19:48,530 --> 00:19:50,350
I hope you have fun playing with it.

399
00:19:50,350 --> 00:19:53,030
- And that's a lie, right? - It's a big, fat whopper.

400
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:56,150
I hope it breaks.

401
00:20:02,820 --> 00:20:03,740
This is a treat.

402
00:20:03,750 --> 00:20:05,760
What brings you guys by?

403
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:09,160
Raj, Howie told me what's going on with you and Lakshmi.

404
00:20:09,370 --> 00:20:10,640
You told her?

405
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:12,420
I told everybody.

406
00:20:14,610 --> 00:20:17,300
We believe there's someone out there who will love you for you.

407
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:20,090
Actually, we kind of agreed to disagree on that one,

408
00:20:20,090 --> 00:20:23,480
but we both think you shouldn't marry this woman.

409
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:26,360
So, while I'm waiting for this mysterious perfect match

410
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:29,750
who may or may not exist, I'm supposed to just be alone?

411
00:20:29,830 --> 00:20:31,500
Not necessarily.

412
00:20:31,610 --> 00:20:35,700
I think we found someone for you to cuddle with.

413
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:39,370
Oh, my goodness.

414
00:20:39,370 --> 00:20:43,590
Aren't you the cutest little Yorkie ever!

415
00:20:44,940 --> 00:20:46,260
You got him for me?

416
00:20:46,270 --> 00:20:49,220
Her. We thought you two would hit it off.

417
00:20:49,220 --> 00:20:51,310
I think we already have.

418
00:20:51,310 --> 00:20:53,500
Thank you guys so much.

419
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:56,590
Let's go see if you fit in my man purse.

420
00:20:59,050 --> 00:21:01,400
Heterosexual, my ass.

